Study Model

A useful way to remember the entire lecture is:

DOCUMENT
   ↓
RETRIEVE
   ↓
GENERATE
   ↓
STRUCTURE
   ↓
CRITIQUE
   ↓
HUMAN REVIEW
   ↓
IMPLEMENT
   ↓
PLAYTEST
   ↓
UPDATE DOCUMENTATION
   ↺

This is the core AI-assisted game-development loop.

────────

Practical Example

Suppose the game needs new shop items.

Step 1 — Source Material

GDD.md
world-lore.md
item-rules.md
style-guide.md

Step 2 — Generator Agent

Prompt:

Read the supplied game documentation.

Generate 10 shop items appropriate to this game.

Each item must include:
- item_id
- name
- description
- price
- gameplay effect
- rarity
- lore justification

Do not introduce mechanics not present in the GDD.

Step 3 — Critic Agent

Evaluate each item against:
- game lore;
- existing mechanics;
- tone;
- balance rules;
- formatting requirements.

Reject items that contradict the documentation.

Step 4 — Human Review

Choose the strongest three.

Step 5 — Structured Export

[
  {
    "item_id": "ITEM_014",
    "name": "Storm Lantern",
    "price": 45,
    "rarity": "common"
  }
]

Step 6 — Game Import

Import the data into the engine and playtest.

This is a simple example of the dynamic content pipeline described in the lesson.

